{"actions":[{"actionCode":"H11100","actionDate":"2025-01-09","source":"House floor actions","text":"Referred to the House Committee on the Judiciary.","type":"IntroReferral"},{"actionCode":"Intro-H","actionDate":"2025-01-09","source":"Library of Congress","text":"Introduced in House","type":"IntroReferral"},{"actionCode":"1000","actionDate":"2025-01-09","source":"Library of Congress","text":"Introduced in House","type":"IntroReferral"}],"congress":119,"congressGovUrl":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-joint-resolution/13","cosponsors":[{"bioguideId":"J000288","fullName":"Rep. Johnson, Henry C. \"Hank\" [D-GA-4]","isOriginalCosponsor":true,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-01-09","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"GA"},{"bioguideId":"L000593","fullName":"Rep. Levin, Mike [D-CA-49]","isOriginalCosponsor":true,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-01-09","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"CA"},{"bioguideId":"L000582","fullName":"Rep. Lieu, Ted [D-CA-36]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-09-09","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"CA"},{"bioguideId":"B001278","fullName":"Rep. Bonamici, Suzanne [D-OR-1]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-12-16","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"OR"},{"bioguideId":"N000147","fullName":"Del. Norton, Eleanor Holmes [D-DC-At Large]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-01-20","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"DC"}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-17T15:26:46+00:00","id":"hjres13-119","introducedDate":"2025-01-09","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-01-09","text":"Referred to the House Committee on the Judiciary."},"laws":[],"number":"13","originChamber":"House","policyArea":"Crime and Law Enforcement","sponsors":[{"bioguideId":"C001068","district":9,"fullName":"Rep. Cohen, Steve [D-TN-9]","party":"D","state":"TN"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2025-01-09","actionDesc":"Introduced in House","text":"<p>This joint resolution proposes a constitutional amendment limiting the pardon power of the President.</p><p>The amendment prohibits the President from granting a pardon or reprieve to himself or herself, to relatives or members of the administration, to paid campaign employees, to a person or entity for an offense motivated by an interest of any of those people, or to a person or entity for an offense directed by or coordinated with the President.</p><p>The amendment also invalidates pardons issued for a corrupt purpose.</p>","updateDate":"2025-02-03T16:22:40Z","versionCode":"00"}],"title":"Proposing an amendment to the Constitution of the United States limiting the pardon power of the President.","type":"hjres","updateDate":"2026-01-21T09:05:16Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2026-01-21T09:05:16Z"}
